 },
 "scenes": {
  "1": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "A basic logistic regression separates",
     "adults with and without diabetes"
    ],
    "start": 1.8,
    "end": 6.368
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "at an AUC of 0.961."
    ],
    "start": 6.368,
    "end": 8.595
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "From survey data alone,",
     "that is suspiciously high."
    ],
    "start": 9.845,
    "end": 13.302
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "I'm [Name];",
     "I led governance and integration."
    ],
    "start": 13.302,
    "end": 16.702
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "[Name] led data quality and preparation,"
    ],
    "start": 16.702,
    "end": 19.551
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "[Name] exploration, labels and bias,",
     "and [Name] modelling and conclusions."
    ],
    "start": 19.551,
    "end": 24.405
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "We present in that order,",
     "and the 0.961 runs through the whole talk."
    ],
    "start": 24.405,
    "end": 28.9
   }
  ],
  "2": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "Our question: who gets labelled diabetic,",
     "and what do preparation decisions change?"
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 5.883
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "The design: one L2 logistic regression",
     "on three preparations of the same data,"
    ],
    "start": 5.883,
    "end": 11.282
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "naive, minimal and systematic,"
    ],
    "start": 11.282,
    "end": 13.518
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "scored on all adults",
     "and on adults not yet diagnosed."
    ],
    "start": 13.518,
    "end": 16.895
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Our research questions:",
     "what does the label measure?"
    ],
    "start": 17.945,
    "end": 21.227
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Is the high AUC leakage?"
    ],
    "start": 21.227,
    "end": 23.348
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Does systematic preparation pay?"
    ],
    "start": 23.348,
    "end": 25.9
   }
  ],
  "3": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "The data: NHANES 2021 to 2023,",
     "the CDC's national health survey."
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 4.847
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Our cohort is 5,730 non-pregnant adults",
     "with an HbA1c result."
    ],
    "start": 4.847,
    "end": 9.406
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "The label is positive",
     "for a self-reported diagnosis,"
    ],
    "start": 9.406,
    "end": 12.021
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "or HbA1c of 6.5 percent or more."
    ],
    "start": 12.021,
    "end": 14.731
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Survey-weighted,",
     "14.0 percent are positive."
    ],
    "start": 14.731,
    "end": 17.9
   }
  ],
  "4": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "Governance came first.",
     "The NCHS data use agreement forbids"
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 4.196
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "re-identification and linkage,",
     "so we did neither."
    ],
    "start": 4.196,
    "end": 7.66
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "We kept 78 of 175 columns,",
     "verified every raw file by hash,"
    ],
    "start": 7.66,
    "end": 13.204
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "and locked our hypotheses by hash",
     "before running any model."
    ],
    "start": 13.204,
    "end": 17.1
   }
  ],
  "5": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "To check our survey-weighting code,",
     "we re-ran NCHS Data Brief 516:"
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 4.228
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "total prevalence 15.79 percent",
     "against the published 15.8,"
    ],
    "start": 4.228,
    "end": 8.135
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "and all 27 published",
     "estimates match closely."
    ],
    "start": 8.135,
    "end": 10.9
   }
  ],
  "6": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "Correct numbers can still mislead."
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 2.327
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "In [Name]'s analysis,"
    ],
    "start": 2.327,
    "end": 3.901
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "insured adults show 5.3 points",
     "more diabetes than the uninsured."
    ],
    "start": 3.901,
    "end": 8.572
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "That is confounding by age:",
     "the insured are much older."
    ],
    "start": 8.572,
    "end": 12.322
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Age-standardised,"
    ],
    "start": 12.322,
    "end": 13.489
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "the gap falls to 0.7 points,",
     "and its interval includes zero."
    ],
    "start": 13.489,
    "end": 17.7
   }
  ],
  "7": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "Most unexpected for me: of six hypotheses",
     "locked before we saw any related data,"
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 6.476
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "only three were supported."
    ],
    "start": 6.476,
    "end": 8.167
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Now [Name] asks whether",
     "the data deserve the same trust."
    ],
    "start": 9.417,
    "end": 12.9
   }
  ],
  "8": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "I'm [Name];",
     "I led data quality and preparation."
    ],
    "start": 1.5,
    "end": 4.898
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "I profiled before cleaning."
    ],
    "start": 4.898,
    "end": 6.736
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "NHANES stores 'refused' and 'don't know'",
     "as numeric codes such as 7, 9, 77 and 99."
    ],
    "start": 6.736,
    "end": 13.011
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "The common shortcut sets those values",
     "to missing in every column."
    ],
    "start": 13.011,
    "end": 16.648
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "That catches 57 genuine codes,",
     "and destroys 1,496 valid measurements,"
    ],
    "start": 16.648,
    "end": 22.523
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "including HbA1c",
     "values of exactly 7.0 percent."
    ],
    "start": 22.523,
    "end": 26.7
   }
  ],
  "9": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "Each 7.0 is above the 6.5 threshold:",
     "a diabetes case."
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 4.48
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "The shortcut erased 29 of 721",
     "HbA1c-based positives."
    ],
    "start": 4.48,
    "end": 9.435
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Only six changed label;"
    ],
    "start": 10.685,
    "end": 12.145
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "the rest had also self-reported,",
     "so the either-or label hid the damage."
    ],
    "start": 12.145,
    "end": 16.009
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "No summary statistic shows this."
    ],
    "start": 16.009,
    "end": 17.9
   }
  ],
  "10": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "Second, outliers."
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 1.531
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "The 1.5 times IQR rule",
     "flags 542 HbA1c values."
    ],
    "start": 1.531,
    "end": 6.278
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Its upper fence lies above",
     "the diagnostic threshold,"
    ],
    "start": 7.328,
    "end": 9.691
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "so the 519 high values are diabetes",
     "by definition: the disease, not errors."
    ],
    "start": 9.691,
    "end": 15.138
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "We reviewed and kept them all."
    ],
    "start": 15.138,
    "end": 16.9
   }
  ],
  "11": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "[Name]'s exploration",
     "found redundancy and skew."
    ],
    "start": 1.5,
    "end": 4.202
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Weight and BMI show",
     "severe multicollinearity:"
    ],
    "start": 4.202,
    "end": 7.158
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "variance inflation factors",
     "of 95.7 and 97.6."
    ],
    "start": 7.158,
    "end": 11.203
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Fasting triglycerides are strongly",
     "right-skewed: skewness 6.62."
    ],
    "start": 12.253,
    "end": 16.244
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Both matter for a linear model,"
    ],
    "start": 17.294,
    "end": 19.038
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "so the systematic preparation drops weight",
     "and applies a Yeo-Johnson transform,"
    ],
    "start": 19.038,
    "end": 22.906
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "which brings the skewness close to zero."
    ],
    "start": 22.906,
    "end": 24.9
   }
  ],
  "12": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "Each finding became a switchable step,"
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 3.099
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "fourteen in all, each tied",
     "to its evidence, and none reads the label."
    ],
    "start": 3.099,
    "end": 8.052
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "From them we built three",
     "versions of the data."
    ],
    "start": 9.102,
    "end": 12.416
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Naive keeps every column."
    ],
    "start": 12.416,
    "end": 14.671
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Minimal adds one rule: drop items",
     "that exist only after a diagnosis,"
    ],
    "start": 14.671,
    "end": 20.684
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "such as treatment."
    ],
    "start": 20.684,
    "end": 22.143
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Systematic adds my other steps,"
    ],
    "start": 22.143,
    "end": 24.677
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "from per-variable recoding",
     "to transforms and class weights."
    ],
    "start": 24.677,
    "end": 28.786
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "All three feed the same model",
     "on the same folds."
    ],
    "start": 28.786,
    "end": 32.1
   }
  ],
  "13": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "Most unexpected for me:"
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 1.966
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "one routine cleaning line erased",
     "29 diabetic HbA1c results,"
    ],
    "start": 1.966,
    "end": 6.603
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "and the label hid it."
    ],
    "start": 6.603,
    "end": 7.924
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "But cleaning cannot fix the label itself."
    ],
    "start": 9.174,
    "end": 11.72
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "[Name] shows why."
    ],
    "start": 11.72,
    "end": 12.9
   }
  ],
  "14": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "I'm [Name];",
     "I led exploration, labels and bias."
    ],
    "start": 1.5,
    "end": 4.877
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "First, a fallacy check:",
     "we scanned 224 subgroup comparisons"
    ],
    "start": 4.877,
    "end": 9.603
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "for Simpson's paradox,",
     "and six reversed sign."
    ],
    "start": 9.603,
    "end": 12.236
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "A causal diagram suggests why:",
     "BMI lies between race and diabetes,"
    ],
    "start": 13.486,
    "end": 17.629
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "so adjusting",
     "for it distorts the comparison."
    ],
    "start": 17.629,
    "end": 20.556
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "We report this as exploratory."
    ],
    "start": 20.556,
    "end": 22.9
   }
  ],
  "15": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "Research question one: the label."
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 2.615
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Our label combines two sources,",
     "and they agree substantially"
    ],
    "start": 2.615,
    "end": 5.994
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "but far from perfectly:",
     "Cohen's kappa is 0.70."
    ],
    "start": 5.994,
    "end": 9.673
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Of 819 self-reported diabetics,",
     "250 test below 6.5 percent,"
    ],
    "start": 10.923,
    "end": 17.077
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "and two thirds of those",
     "take insulin or pills."
    ],
    "start": 17.077,
    "end": 19.447
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Treatment lowers",
     "the very marker we label by,"
    ],
    "start": 20.497,
    "end": 23.271
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "so a blood-test-only label",
     "would call treated patients healthy."
    ],
    "start": 23.271,
    "end": 26.9
   }
  ],
  "16": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "The other direction:"
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 1.75
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "152 adults have HbA1c of 6.5 or more",
     "but no diagnosis."
    ],
    "start": 1.75,
    "end": 7.073
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Among adults with high HbA1c,"
    ],
    "start": 8.323,
    "end": 10.58
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "the uninsured are 23.2 percentage points",
     "more often undiagnosed,"
    ],
    "start": 10.58,
    "end": 15.137
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "interval 6.2 to 40.1,",
     "an association from a small subgroup."
    ],
    "start": 15.137,
    "end": 19.652
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "So the label also records access to care."
    ],
    "start": 20.902,
    "end": 23.602
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "That is why we also evaluate",
     "on adults not yet diagnosed:"
    ],
    "start": 23.602,
    "end": 27.159
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "the people screening is for."
    ],
    "start": 27.159,
    "end": 28.9
   }
  ],
  "17": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "The leakage question,",
     "from [Name]'s experiments."
    ],
    "start": 1.5,
    "end": 4.279
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Naive preparation scores an AUC of 0.961."
    ],
    "start": 4.279,
    "end": 7.652
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Minimal preparation removes",
     "only the post-diagnosis items:"
    ],
    "start": 7.652,
    "end": 11.482
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "treatment, diagnosis history",
     "and prior glucose testing."
    ],
    "start": 11.482,
    "end": 14.633
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Same model, same folds: the AUC falls",
     "to 0.828, a paired drop of 0.131."
    ],
    "start": 14.633,
    "end": 19.841
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "A deterioration we wanted:"
    ],
    "start": 21.591,
    "end": 23.563
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "the 0.961 was the label leaking back in,",
     "not skill."
    ],
    "start": 23.563,
    "end": 26.9
   }
  ],
  "18": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "[Name]'s shallow decision tree",
     "shows the mechanism."
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 3.873
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Its root is a treatment item; one branch",
     "then splits on age at diagnosis."
    ],
    "start": 3.873,
    "end": 8.966
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "But 86 percent were never asked"
    ],
    "start": 8.966,
    "end": 11.895
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "that question, and median imputation",
     "filled every blank with 50."
    ],
    "start": 11.895,
    "end": 16.833
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "So 'age 50' became a code",
     "for 'never diagnosed'."
    ],
    "start": 18.083,
    "end": 21.9
   }
  ],
  "19": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "Most unexpected for me:"
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 1.853
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "at one shared threshold, the model flags",
     "70 of every 100 diagnosed diabetics,"
    ],
    "start": 1.853,
    "end": 6.626
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "but only 52 of 100 undiagnosed ones."
    ],
    "start": 6.626,
    "end": 9.818
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "[Name] takes the last question."
    ],
    "start": 11.068,
    "end": 12.9
   }
  ],
  "20": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "I'm [Name];",
     "I led modelling and conclusions."
    ],
    "start": 1.5,
    "end": 4.293
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Last question:",
     "does systematic preparation pay?"
    ],
    "start": 4.293,
    "end": 7.26
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Same model, minimal against systematic:"
    ],
    "start": 7.26,
    "end": 9.802
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "AUC rises by 0.008,",
     "interval 0.000 to 0.016."
    ],
    "start": 9.802,
    "end": 14.985
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Our smallest effect of interest,",
     "fixed in advance, was 0.01."
    ],
    "start": 16.435,
    "end": 20.448
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "The interval covers both no gain",
     "and a worthwhile one,"
    ],
    "start": 20.448,
    "end": 23.214
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "so the result is inconclusive:",
     "underpowered, not evidence of no effect."
    ],
    "start": 23.214,
    "end": 27.9
   }
  ],
  "21": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "One step did harm."
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 1.506
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "From minimal to systematic,",
     "the Brier score worsens by 0.074."
    ],
    "start": 1.506,
    "end": 6.039
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "The cause is [Name]'s class weights:"
    ],
    "start": 7.289,
    "end": 8.999
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "the systematic model predicts",
     "an average risk of 41 percent"
    ],
    "start": 8.999,
    "end": 13.232
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "where the observed rate is 17."
    ],
    "start": 13.232,
    "end": 15.849
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Removing only the class weights",
     "restores calibration"
    ],
    "start": 15.849,
    "end": 18.872
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "and leaves AUC 0.007 above minimal."
    ],
    "start": 18.872,
    "end": 22.9
   }
  ],
  "22": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "Who does the score serve? On all adults,",
     "the systematic model scores 0.836;"
    ],
    "start": 1.5,
    "end": 5.951
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "on adults not yet diagnosed, 0.781."
    ],
    "start": 5.951,
    "end": 8.379
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "84 percent of positives",
     "were already diagnosed,"
    ],
    "start": 9.829,
    "end": 12.926
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "so the all-adults AUC mostly",
     "measures recognition: spectrum bias."
    ],
    "start": 12.926,
    "end": 16.9
   }
  ],
  "23": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "Next, drop two items",
     "that mark earlier contact with a doctor."
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 4.034
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "On all adults, AUC falls by 0.016."
    ],
    "start": 4.034,
    "end": 7.555
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "On adults not yet diagnosed,"
    ],
    "start": 7.555,
    "end": 9.403
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "it rises by 0.019,",
     "interval 0.004 to 0.034:"
    ],
    "start": 9.403,
    "end": 14.946
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "consistent with recognition",
     "and screening pulling apart."
    ],
    "start": 14.946,
    "end": 18.28
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "But the lower end lies inside our margin,",
     "so it is inconclusive."
    ],
    "start": 19.53,
    "end": 23.9
   }
  ],
  "24": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "An internal hold-out of 1,146 adults,"
    ],
    "start": 0.3,
    "end": 4.198
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "scored once, repeats the leakage drop",
     "and the inconclusive preparation result."
    ],
    "start": 4.198,
    "end": 8.683
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "So, three answers."
    ],
    "start": 8.683,
    "end": 9.982
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "The label records care as well as disease."
    ],
    "start": 9.982,
    "end": 12.193
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "The 0.961 was leakage, not skill."
    ],
    "start": 13.243,
    "end": 15.417
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "Systematic preparation barely moved AUC;",
     "its value was valid data kept"
    ],
    "start": 16.467,
    "end": 21.264
   },
   {
    "lines": [
     "and an honest test",
     "on adults not yet diagnosed."
    ],
    "start": 21.264,
    "end": 24.1
   }
  ],
  "25": [
   {
    "lines": [
     "Most unexpected for me:"
    ],
